# Line endings.
#
# Git for Windows ships with core.autocrlf=true, so a fresh clone there rewrites
# every tracked file to CRLF in the working tree. gofmt writes LF and compares
# bytes, so it then reports all 61 Go files as unformatted — and a contributor
# on Windows cannot tell a real formatting problem from an artifact of their
# checkout. `gofmt -l` stops being usable as a gate.
#
# eol=lf overrides core.autocrlf per file, so this holds regardless of how any
# individual machine is configured, and keeps diffs free of whole-file rewrites
# when the same repo is edited from more than one platform.
#
# The repo is all text — Go, Markdown, go.mod/go.sum, a Makefile — so there is
# nothing to exempt.
* text=auto eol=lf
